WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.260
Here are the steps for attaching
the four color changer on a DM-80.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.720
The first thing to recognize is
that the fasteners that attach both

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:14.220
the extension plate and the color
changer itself are in two parts.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.860
There's a threaded post
and a threaded nut.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.780
If you remove the nut, sometimes
the threaded post will also be removed.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.860
Use a screwdriver to separate them.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.500
When installing the extension plate or
the color changer,

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:35.540
first insert and tighten the threaded
post, then attach the threaded nut,

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:40.560
leaving it loose enough to slip
the attachments with their openings.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.980
The extension and the color
changer will be attached here.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:49.240
Then, tighten the nuts
to secure the attachments.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:59.920
The four-color changer also requires
this curved cam with three screws.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.410
the cam has three parts connected
with those three screws.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.840
Loosen the screws and attach the cam

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:14.720
to the bed by inserting the round
rod into the slot of the bed.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:19.240
Slide it to the left until it
stops and then tighten the screws.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.160
When the four-color changer is installed,
it fits snugly against that curved cam.

